Z||000000||Dave85||12-22-1999||06:32 PM||||<BR>I know this is not exactly Fiero related but I'm curious. Any Skydivers on the forum?  <BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||12-22-1999||07:54 PM||||I'm a pilot.  I've been asked by many people why would you want to jump out of a perfectly good airplane?  I still think it would be fun and intend to do my first jump this spring when the weather is a little warmer.  I know there are some really hard core guys who jump year round, but it's just too cold for me.  Yesterday it was 21 degrees out and when I was out flying I heard on the unicom frequency "Jumpers away at 10,000ft".  They must be mad to even entertain the notion of falling at 120mph in below zero air temperatures.  Wonder what the wind chill is on that jump (-200)?||||reg||10
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||10:58 PM||||I was Airborne when I was in the Army.  What a rush! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But since then, I've grown much wiser (the medication helps with that, I think) and have decided to keep my feet planted firmly on the ground.  The worst I can do if I fall down here is dislocate my shoulder.  (Once again, I know this from experience! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000003||dogtired||12-23-1999||04:49 AM||||I wanna be an Airborne Ranger<BR>I wanna live a life of Danger!<P>"NOT"<P>I also have a Single engine land license, but still can't figure why anyone would try to fly? Without wings? Without motor? Without Drugs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I do think the para-gliders are COOL.<P>But Ill ask? Dave85, are you 85? and are you a JUMPER? To each their own, Watch out for that flag poleeeeeeee   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||deceler8||12-23-1999||09:35 AM||||Yeah, I was too, the operative word being "was".<P>My last jump was in Michigan in 1988...October on a warm day...<P>While the plane was gaining altitude, a wind shift came through and everyone had to jump. The plane had no seats so it couldn't land with jumpers aboard so we all had to leave.<P>From 6,000 feet I landed about two miles away from the target after missing power lines and trees. After the two mile walk back to the airport through muddy soybean fields dragging my chute, I decided that was enough of a headrush for a while.<P>I do miss it, though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave85||12-23-1999||10:10 AM||||FLYING has been a life long passion for me. I took flying lessons and soloed on my 16th birthday. I always wanted to skydive but never got the chance until about 2 years ago. I drove 2 hrs. to do a tandem jump and have always wanted to learn to skydive. The time is here! Things have worked out and I'm starting school this weekend. <P>BTW 85 is not my age, although I do feel 85 once in a while. I refers to my Fiero. I drive a black 85 GT.<P>Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||12-25-1999||04:31 AM||||My dad was an Airborn and was a skydiving instructor a while back, but all the stopped when he snapped a tendon in his knee waterskiing.  I really want to skydive!  I hope I can start this summer...||||reg||14
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||06:53 PM||||You know, sometimes "flying" can be a way of life. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||12-26-1999||09:17 PM||||I have never done anything that was worthwhile that didn't involve a certain amount of risk! adrenalin is my friend. ||||reg||7
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-27-1999||01:09 AM||||Maybe, but Prozac can be your best friend. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Scott2M4||12-27-1999||12:56 PM||||I did static line jumping two or three times back in 1994.  Shortly after that, the kids came along so I decided I'd postpone the inevitable.<P>I do miss it, though.  The first time I did it, I was scared to death!  But, after letting go of the wing strut, and making sure all cells were full and the risers were functioning properly, I "sat back" and enjoyed myself.  It turned out to be 15 <B>INCREDIBLE</B> minutes!!!!!<P>Like other things, I'd recommend it to someone to try (at least) once.||||reg||1
